## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a real-time, privacy-conscious counterfactual evaluation path that handles opt-out scenarios without leaking data or breaking latency SLAs. Focuses API ergonomics, data modeling, privacy controls, and safe rollout strategies.

## Key Concepts

- Counterfactual evaluation under variable consent
- Data minimization and redaction in feature vectors
- Idempotent API design and fault handling
- Canary rollouts, drift detection, and rollback mechanisms
- Privacy-preserving audit logging and attestations

## Code Example

```javascript
// Validate payload for counterfactual enqueue
function validateCounterfactualPayload(p){
  const required = ['user_id','scenario_id','model_version','timestamp'];
  for (const k of required) if (!p[k]) throw new Error(`Missing ${k}`);
  // optional: ensure scenario_id is UUID, timestamp is recent
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you ensure data minimization for the counterfactual features?
- How would you implement drift-detection metrics for counterfactual vs current scores?

